                                                                                                   XSS Testing (POST-Based)

✅ Where to Test:
•	On any website’s input fields
•	Especially on pages where you submit a form
•	This is called stored xss

How to Test:
1.	Find input fields like:
o	Name
o	Email
o	Address
o	Comment boxes , search bar’s etc..

2.	Enter XSS payload in the field (e.g. name)
              <script>alert('XSS')</script>

3.	Submit the form (usually sends data via POST request).

4.	After submission, if the input reflects back unsanitized → payload executes.

 Example:
•	Website: http://testphp.vulnweb.com/
•	Login and go to profile update section.
•	Enter payload in name field: <script>alert('XSS')</script>
•	Click Update
•	If the site is vulnerable, the page will show a popup after update, confirming XSS.


